                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you're reading this, buy the game.  Its been criminally overlooked.\n\nThis game is actually well designed.  Its fully complete with a main quest line, an end game, and multiple endings to include a 'second quest' of sorts that's too good to spoil.  \n\nIn addition, there are several additional features that further enrich the game.  You can cycle recruited characters at a guild.  There's a hometown to improve by recruiting immigrants over the course of the game.  You can buy a house, get married, have children, decorate your home, grow food, and cook meals to permanently improve your characters in the end-game.\n\nFinally, the english translation is fabulously awful in the best possible way.  And there are long cut scenes dubbed with music in Japanese with subtitles that make absolutely no sense.  Its unintentionally laugh-out-loud funny because the developer obviously put his heart and soul into this one...and he doesn't miss the mark.\n\nDon't get me wrong, its a relatively small, low-budget game.  Its not going win any awards.  But its totally worth the money.  I'll buy from this developer again.",
